11.0.0 — preset menus for the drums and the sampler when they play inside another app

New since 10085, built by the Echoel Studio run; nothing here is device-verified yet.
- Drums as a plugin in another app (for example AUM): its preset menu lists six kits — Init, Tight,
  Deep, Bright, Long Kick and Soft. Init is the sound a newly loaded plugin makes.
- Sampler as a plugin in another app: its preset menu lists six shapes — Init, Tight, Soft Start,
  Swell, Long Tail and One-Shot (attack, release, level and mode). Choosing one never retunes the
  sample: its root key stays where you set it.
- Underneath: every built-in instrument is now tested to keep its pitch and length at 44.1, 48 and
  96 kHz, the rates a host app may run at.
Limits as in 10085: several notes are chosen with the Select More switch, not by drawing a frame;
the note editor zooms in four sizes; the drum step grid has no zoom strip yet; a sample click above
300 BPM is cut by the next one.

Previous: 10085. A green commit that changes this file uploads build 10000 + run number. A test
list, not a source for claims (ContentPipeline/CLAIMS.md).

One ask, as for 10083 to 10085. Start a screen recording, open the app, and try to make sixteen
bars in two to five minutes: a beat, a bass line or a chord, then Play. No list and no protocol; stop wherever
it stops being possible or pleasant. The recording is the answer. What gets in the way in it is
the next work, in the order it happened.

The five checks of 10079 stay open and unchanged and rest until that recording exists.
